      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/Capability",
      "localId": "deploy-access",
      "name": "Deployment Access",
      "description": "Credentials and configuration to deploy this layer — the OAuth client id/secret and cookie secret that deploy/.env holds. Probed by CONFIGURATION rather than by attempting a deployment, the same reading signing-api takes: a probe that tried to deploy would be indistinguishable from an outage, and would act on an external host just to answer a question about setup. The path is not invented — deploy/deploy.sh gates on exactly this file ([ ! -f \"$DEPLOY_DIR/.env\" ]) before it will run, so the probe agrees with the script it describes. Declared 2026-09-20, bean folio-assistant-q6ud: it was referenced by deployment-auth and declared by nothing, which executing the degradation model found on its first run.",
      "detection": {
        "method": "file-exists",
        "path": "cat-harness/deploy/.env"
      },
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/capability/deploy-access"
    }
  ]
